### Classification

The previous checkpoints established that ServiceNow already provides:
- workflow orchestration;
- AI agents;
- multi-agent workflows;
- human supervision;
- execution state;
- execution history;
- workflow context;
- cross-system actions;
- live collaboration;
- state synchronization;
- playbooks;
- auditability.
The question now is narrower:
> **Does a residual execution-intelligence layer remain above ServiceNow's existing workflow and agentic capabilities that ART could legitimately occupy?**
The test specifically examines:
EXECUTION STATE
+
DECISION PROVENANCE
+
ACTION PROVENANCE
+
STATE-TRANSITION REASONING
+
CROSS-SYSTEM CONTEXT
+
INTERRUPTION / RECOVERY
+
HUMAN-AGENT-SYSTEM CONTINUITY
+
EXECUTION MEMORY
The standard is intentionally high.

evidence.statement:
ServiceNow's in-product agentic experience allows users to:
- monitor active agentic workflows;
- answer follow-up questions;
- approve steps;
- provide input;
- review historical runs.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/in-product-agentic-ai.html

ServiceNow's Customer Service Management AI-agent collection includes a **Triage Cases** agentic workflow covering:
- validation;
- case creation;
- verification;
- escalation;
- context retrieval;
- customer inquiries.
Sources:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/customer-service-management/now-assist-for-csm/case-resolving-use-case.html
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/customer-service-management/now-assist-for-csm/csm-ai-agents-use-cases.html

When AI determines that a request clearly meets approval criteria, ServiceNow:
1. creates an approval record;
2. sets the approval state to Approved;
3. adds a comment explaining how the decision was made;
4. updates related human approvals waiting on the same decision to No Longer Required.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/build-workflows/explore-intelligent-approvals.html

ServiceNow identifies an explicit **Approval user** role for requests AI cannot confidently evaluate.
Approval users:
- handle requests that AI cannot decide;
- receive work notes about the AI attempt;
- make the approval decision;
- can review audit trails of automatic approvals.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/build-workflows/explore-intelligent-approvals.html

The broader ServiceNow agentic platform supports human supervision inside agentic workflows.
The in-product agentic experience allows users to:
- monitor active workflows;
- answer follow-up questions;
- approve next steps;
- provide additional input;
- inspect processing messages;
- view step completion;
- review previous runs.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/in-product-agentic-ai.html

ServiceNow's AI Workflows panel displays:
- active agentic workflows on records;
- execution state;
- responsible users;
- processing status;
- progress;
- previous executions;
- questions requiring input;
- final outputs.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/in-product-agentic-ai.html

The Intelligent Approvals homepage exposes decision counts including:
- total decisions;
- total auto-approved;
- total auto-rejected;
- total undecided.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/zurich/build-workflows/explore-intelligent-approvals.html

The public documentation does not establish:
- average time from "can't decide" to human decision;
- number of context switches;
- number of participants normally involved;
- frequency of multi-person collaboration;
- number of external systems consulted;
- frequency of clarification requests;
- time spent reconstructing evidence;
- decision quality;
- downstream rework;
- exception-resolution cost.

ServiceNow's Vulnerability Response exception management explicitly covers:
- exception requests for remediation tasks;
- exception requests for vulnerable items;
- exception rules;
- false positives;
- approval rules;
- multiple approval levels.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/vulnerability-response/exception-mgt-approval-rules.html

ServiceNow Customer Service Management provides another strong participation pattern.
When a case or account is escalated, the escalation request can contain:
- reason;
- justification;
- severity;
- escalation template;
- watch list;
- assignment group;
- assigned agent.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/customer-service-management/escalate-csm-case.html

The evidence does **not** establish that an Intelligent Approvals "can't decide" case routinely involves:
- multiple humans simultaneously;
- an agent and humans collaborating in real time;
- multiple external systems;
- live evidence gathering;
- synchronous discussion;
- complex state reconstruction;
- concurrent actions;
- cross-system execution.

The strongest documented scenario is **ServiceNow Major Incident Management**, particularly the current Major Incident Workbench / Service Operations Workspace workflow.
This is stronger than the Intelligent Approvals example for testing the ART proposition because ServiceNow explicitly documents:
- multiple resolver groups;
- major incident managers;
- communication managers;
- stakeholders;
- conference calls;
- chat;
- incident tasks;
- communication plans;
- state changes;
- coordinated remediation;
- real-time collaboration.
Sources:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/incident-management/major-incident-workbench.html
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/incident-management/major-incident-management.html
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/service-operations-workspace/mim-process-sow.html

ServiceNow documents multiple ways to create or promote a major incident candidate:
- propose an incident as a major incident candidate;
- create a major incident candidate;
- promote based on configured major-incident trigger rules;
- create a major incident directly.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/incident-management/major-incident-management.html

The Major Incident Workbench is explicitly designed for:
- major incident managers;
- communication managers;
- resolver groups.
The workbench aggregates information from:
- assignment group;
- assigned-to fields;
- incident communication plan;
- incident tasks;
- active conference calls.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/incident-management/major-incident-workbench.html

ServiceNow's Major Security Incident Management workspace can track collaboration activity from Microsoft Teams and Microsoft SharePoint.
The documentation states that:
- Teams chat and SharePoint files/folders are used for coordination;
- collaboration activity is posted back to the major security incident;
- SharePoint file and folder updates are synchronized with the workspace;
- activity is reflected in the incident activity stream.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/security-incident-response/collab-tab.html

We have not demonstrated:
- ART is faster;
- ART creates better coordination;
- ART preserves more useful context;
- ART reduces handoffs;
- ART improves decision quality;
- ART improves recovery;
- ART reduces resolution time;
- ART improves agent-human interaction;
- customers need ART;
- customers would pay for ART.

ServiceNow's Incident Assist agentic workflow uses specialist AI agents to retrieve:
- incident context;
- SLA information;
- configuration items;
- changes;
- outages;
- problems;
- child incidents;
- on-call experts;
- caller history;
- caller assets;
- similar resolved incidents.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/now-assist-for-it-service-management-itsm/now-assist-itsm-incident-assist-workflow.html

ServiceNow also documents a security-incident resolution agentic workflow that can:
- retrieve incident details;
- retrieve knowledge articles;
- retrieve similar closed incidents;
- generate a resolution plan;
- execute resolution assistance;
- use multiple specialist AI agents.
Sources:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/now-assist-for-security-incident-response-sir/resolve-sir-incident-aiagent.html
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/security-management/now-assist-for-security-incident-response-sir/now-assist-sir-resolve-incident-ai-workflow.html

ServiceNow also provides an agentic workflow for generating post-incident reviews.
The AI agent can retrieve:
- incident details;
- assignment information;
- service and CI;
- resolution notes;
- business impact;
- activity logs;
- work notes;
- related records.
The generated report can be reviewed and revised before being finalized into the major incident record.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/it-service-management/now-assist-for-it-service-management-itsm/now-assist-itsm-aiagents-mim-usecase.html

Current ServiceNow documentation describes agentic workflows as AI-driven workflow orchestrations that can use one or more AI agents to dynamically plan, execute and adapt actions based on context, data and intermediate results.
They can:
- coordinate multiple AI agents and skills;
- gather information;
- reason over data;
- take actions;
- verify results;
- adapt execution paths;
- operate across systems and records.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/sn-aia-use-cases-list.html

ServiceNow provides detailed execution information for agentic workflows.
Users can inspect:
- processing messages;
- steps already completed;
- steps still in progress;
- previous answers to follow-up questions;
- final outputs;
- sources behind AI reasoning.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/in-product-agentic-ai.html

ServiceNow's traditional workflow engine also maintains a Workflow Context.
The Workflow Context maintains:
- state of the overall process;
- state of individual activities;
- results of completed activities;
- execution path;
- active and historical workflow contexts.
It can display:
- workflow timeline;
- graphical execution path;
- activity states;
- execution order;
- execution time;
- error data.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/r_AdministeringWorkflowContexts.html

ServiceNow Workflow Studio provides runtime information for flows, subflows and actions.
It exposes:
- current state;
- executed items;
- data produced during execution;
- context records;
- flow logs.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/build-workflows/workflow-studio/flow-execution-details.html

ServiceNow agentic workflows can adapt execution paths based on:
- conditions;
- findings;
- system responses;
- intermediate results.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/sn-aia-use-cases-list.html
Workflow Context also records the actual path taken through a workflow.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/r_AdministeringWorkflowContexts.html

No customer-specific production workflow has been obtained.
No executable ART + ServiceNow environment has been established.
Therefore this checkpoint evaluates:
- official ServiceNow architecture;
- documented workflow composition;
- execution contexts;
- subflow relationships;
- execution timelines;
- agentic workflow history;
- AI-agent memory.
It does **not** establish:
- actual customer usage;
- actual customer pain;
- actual performance;
- actual ART superiority;
- willingness to pay.

ServiceNow Workflow Studio supports reusable subflows.
A subflow can be called by:
- another flow;
- another subflow;
- a playbook;
- a script.
Subflows receive defined inputs and return defined outputs.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/build-workflows/workflow-studio/subflows.html

Workflow Studio stores flow execution details in a flow context record.
The context includes:
- flow outcome state;
- runtime duration;
- flow log messages;
- configuration;
- runtime values.
Each flow run receives its own execution context.
ServiceNow supports states including:
- Complete;
- In Progress;
- Waiting;
- Canceled;
- Error.
When waiting, the flow is quiesced and serialized into a context record.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/build-workflows/workflow-studio/flow-designer-arch-overview.html

ServiceNow's Workflow Context maintains:
- overall process state;
- individual activity state;
- results of completed activities;
- execution path through the process.
The workflow context canvas provides a visual representation of that path.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/servicenow-platform/legacy-workflow/r_AdministeringWorkflowContexts.html

ServiceNow's current agentic workflow experience provides:
- execution state;
- processing messages;
- execution history;
- previous answers to follow-up questions;
- final outputs;
- sources behind reasoning;
- human supervision;
- AI-modified field indicators.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/in-product-agentic-ai.html

ServiceNow describes agentic workflows as capable of:
- achieving outcomes rather than single tasks;
- coordinating multiple AI agents and skills;
- adapting to variability;
- operating across systems and records;
- reading data;
- updating records;
- triggering downstream actions.
Source:
https://www.servicenow.com/docs/r/intelligent-experiences/sn-aia-use-cases-list.html

