## 1. Research Question
The previous checkpoints established:
SERVICE NOW
↓
EXCEPTION
↓
HUMAN PARTICIPATION
and then established that ServiceNow already supports:
- ad-hoc approvers;
- approval groups;
- escalation;
- reassignment;
- multi-level approvals;
- watch lists;
- dynamic approvers;
- case/account escalation.
The critical question for this checkpoint is now:
> **Can we reconstruct a documented ServiceNow scenario in which an exception becomes a genuinely live, multi-participant, state-changing coordination problem?**
The investigation must determine whether the resulting live coordination is already handled by ServiceNow's native capabilities.

